# Every file here is an artifact whose bytes matter. prompt.md is generated from
# sources/ byte for byte, and it carries no CR anywhere: the CRLF that
# claude-muse.cmd needs on Windows is an instruction in the prose, not a
# property of the block. Line-ending conversion on checkout would rewrite the
# prompt and fail the build check on a Windows clone.
#
# This setting stops Git from converting; it cannot stop an editor from saving
# CRLF in the first place. build.cjs refuses such a source, and check.cjs
# refuses a prompt that carries a CR, so the invariant is enforced rather than
# merely requested.
* -text
